      "id": "e035b533-f4ad-475b-97b7-bb50ddeef07d",
      "name": "User Query"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $json.text }}\n\n",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "=You are a battery/laptop identification assistant for a battery sales business in Pakistan. Customer messages may be in English, Urdu, or Roman Urdu (or a mix of all three).  Your job: read the customer's message and extract what battery or laptop model they are asking about. Respond with ONLY a single JSON object \u2014 no explanation, no markdown fences, no extra commentary before or after it.  JSON schema (always return every key, use null where not applicable): {   \"query_type\": \"battery_model\" | \"laptop_model\" | \"unclear\",   \"raw_text\": \"<the original customer text, unchanged>\",   \"extracted_model\": \"<battery model/part number if directly mentioned, else null>\",   \"laptop_brand\": \"<e.g. HP, Dell, Lenovo \u2014 null if not applicable>\",   \"laptop_series\": \"<e.g. EliteBook 840 G5 \u2014 null if not applicable>\",   \"confidence\": <float between 0.0 and 1.0>,   \"notes\": \"<short note explaining your reasoning, one sentence max>\" }  Rules: 1. If the customer gives an exact battery part number or model code (e.g. HT03XL,    854108-855), set query_type to \"battery_model\" and put the exact string they used in    extracted_model. Set confidence high (0.85+). 2. If the customer only gives a laptop brand/model with no battery part number (e.g. \"HP    EliteBook 840 G5 battery available hai?\"), set query_type to \"laptop_model\", fill in    laptop_brand and laptop_series, and leave extracted_model as null. 3. If the message is too vague to determine either (e.g. \"battery chahiye\", \"need a    battery\"), set query_type to \"unclear\" and confidence below 0.5. Do not guess a brand    or model that wasn't stated or clearly implied. 4. Never invent, complete, or \"correct\" a part number the customer didn't actually write.    If they wrote it slightly wrong, pass it through as-is in extracted_model \u2014 matching    against the real inventory happens in a later step, not here. 5. Ignore small talk, greetings, or pricing questions unrelated to model identification \u2014    focus only on identifying the product. 6. Output raw JSON only. Do not wrap it in ```json code fences. Do not add any text before    or after the JSON object. USER MESSAGE:\n{{$json.text}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        672,
        192
      ],
      "id": "d608e945-7700-45ed-9fe0-100d1fe4bd34",
      "name": "LLM Extarcting the Required data from raw text"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const json = $input.first().json;\nlet raw = json.text || json.output || json.content || json.message;\nif (raw && typeof raw === 'object') {\n  raw = JSON.stringify(raw);\n}\nif (!raw) {\n  return [{ json: { valid: false, error: 'no_text_returned', raw: '' } }];\n}\nconst cleaned = String(raw).replace(/```json/g, '').replace(/```/g, '').trim();\nlet parsed;\ntry {\n  parsed = JSON.parse(cleaned);\n} catch {\n  return [{ json: { valid: false, error: 'parse_failed', raw: cleaned } }];\n}\nreturn [{ json: { valid: true, ...parsed } }];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1024,
        192
      ],
